A||N||1||FieroFanaticus2||'Whinning' Noise during start up.  Now Dead.||||1||
Z||000000||FieroFanaticus2||09-07-2001||09:51 PM||||Well I went out to start fo the fiero and while I was starting it up it made this god awful whinning noise.  It reminded me of an old man wheezing.  I drove it to where I was going and let it sit for about 2 hours.  When I came back to drive home it did the same this on start up, but drives just fine once started.  When I got home and turned it off I thought I would start it up again to see if the wheezing was still there.  So I turned the key and nothing happened.  It didn't start up, nothing.  The Seatbelt light came on, the battery light came on and the check engine light came on, all of which normally happens when it starts up.  Does anybody have any suggestions on what the problem might be??  Maybe the starter, or ignition coils?  HELP!!!<p>[This message has been edited by FieroFanaticus2 (edited 09-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||09-07-2001||10:29 PM||||The starter drive failed to disengauge from the flywheel/flexplate ring gear.<BR>Replace your starter and make sure that it is spaced properly.||||reg||1
